course: dictionary
lesson: 2804
title: Disruptive: causing trouble
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Disruptive means causing trouble so that something cannot go on normally. Look at the words around it for clues. What is being stopped or upset?
explain: «Disruptive behaviour» in class means a pupil keeps interrupting, so others cannot learn. If a sentence says «The storm was disruptive to trains», the storm stopped the trains running as usual. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: The word has a second meaning too. A «disruptive technology» is a new invention that changes a whole business. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning you need.
fact: Disruptive means causing trouble so that something cannot go on normally.
fact: «Disruptive behaviour» means behaviour that stops other people from learning or working.
fact: «Be disruptive to» means to cause problems for something, such as travel.
fact: «Disruptive technology» means a new idea that changes a whole business in a big way.
fact: «Lively» on a school report often means disruptive or hyperactive.
exercise: «The pupil's disruptive behaviour stopped everyone from learning.» What does disruptive mean here? | *Causing trouble so that learning cannot go on | Happy and kind | Helping the teacher | Very quiet and shy
exercise: A new invention changes a whole business. Which word describes it? | *Disruptive | Drooped | Famished | Curt
exercise: «The strike was highly disruptive to travel.» What does highly disruptive mean? | *Caused big problems, so travel could not run as normal | Very quiet and calm | Made travel faster and easier | Lasted only a moment
test: On a school report, «Lively» often means what? | *Disruptive or hyperactive | Quiet and shy | Ancient | Kind and helpful
test: «The storm was disruptive to the ferries.» What does disruptive suggest? | Ferries ran exactly as usual | Ferries were brand new | Ferries were very old | *Ferries could not run as normal
exam: Which sentence uses disruptive to mean changing the usual way things are done? | Grandad said the day was dreich | *A disruptive idea changed the whole way the company sold its goods | The path was treacherous and steep | The pupil talked over the teacher all lesson
